\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0 1.  A bosom friend, the Lord my God is,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Present on earth and in heaven,
\par He knows my worries and my problems
\par And gives me help from heav'n above
\par All power on earth and heavenly power
\par Are given to this heavenly friend of mine.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  To Him is giv'en the name of Jesus
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Because He is the redeemer;
\par He has redeemed me from all my sins
\par And from eternal destruction;
\par O Jesus, Lover and Redeemer
\par You are a wondrous everlasting friend.
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  He is a friend to all humankind
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 As well, the saviour of the world
\par As a result, all draw to His side
\par And taste the sweetness of His love.
\par None can be found so truly friendly,
\par \pard     Comparable to our Lord Jesus Christ.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

